statement:
Let n >= 1, l >= 0, p > n, U any set, V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U with weight mu, H : R^(n+l) -> R^(n+l) any function, z in R^(n+l), and r, rho real with 0 < r <= rho and B_r(z) contained in B_rho(0) (closed balls). Write K(xi, sigma) := V.scaledLpNorm H p xi sigma = (ofReal(sigma^(p-n)) * lower integral over B_sigma(xi) of |H|^p d mu)^(1/p), a value in [0, infinity]. Then:
(K1) K(z, r) <= K(0, rho);
(K2) for every delta >= 0 with K(0, rho) <= ofReal(delta) and mu(B_r(z)) < infinity, the Bochner integral over B_r(z) of |H| d mu is at most delta * rho^(n/p - 1) * mu(B_r(z))^(1 - 1/p), with mu(B_r(z)) taken as a real number.
